This extension adds Star Wars Outlaws modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.

Modders - You can use DTZxPorter's [url=https://dtzxporter.com/tools/hunter]Hunter[/url] to extract game files.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Ubisoft Connect[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Snowdrop ModLoader mods with a "version.dll" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Game Data Folder mods with a "helix" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Game Data Subfolder mods with a "baked", "graph objects" or "game system data" folder install to the "helix" folder.[/*]
[*]ModLoader Plugin mods with a ".dll" or ".asi" file install to the "plugins" folder.[/*]
[*]Config (Documents) mods with a "graphic settings.cfg" file or a ".cfg" file install to the "%USERPROFILE%\Documents\My Games\Outlaws" folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the game folder.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*][size=2][b]The extension will automatically download the [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarsoutlaws/mods/24]Ultimate Star Wars Outlaws Mod Loader[/url]﻿ and install it for the user. [/b][/size][/*]
[*][size=2]On the Ubisoft version, you must have Ubisoft Connect app open when launching the game from Vortex for the game to start.[/size][/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Star Wars Outlaws mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Snowdrop ModLoader:

Recognised when the archive contains a "version.dll" file.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Game Data Folder:

Recognised when the archive contains a "helix" folder.

  Installs to: the game folder

========================================================================

Game Data Subfolder:

Recognised when the archive contains a "baked", "graph objects" or "game system data" folder.

  Installs to: "helix"

========================================================================

ModLoader Plugin:

Recognised when the archive contains a ".dll" or ".asi" file.

  Installs to: "plugins"

========================================================================

Config File Mods:

Configuration tweaks, deployed to the game's config location.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file named "graphic settings.cfg".
    - Recognised by any file with the ".cfg" extension.

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\Documents\My Games\Outlaws"

  Common mistakes:
    - Shipping a config file with one of these names inside an unrelated mod makes the whole archive install as a config mod.

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

The catch-all. Any archive that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied across unchanged.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report the mod as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

